\title{hyperannotatR: Region-of-Interest Annotation for Hyperspectral Data}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Annotate multiple layers of regions of interest in hyperspectral data cubes and their associated display rasters. Annotations are stored as validated simple-feature geometries in image pixel coordinates with explicit pyramid-level transforms, and can be rasterised to binary, labelled, or multi-class integer masks for downstream segmentation and classification workflows. A batch annotation application built on 'shiny' supports resumable sessions across image queues, live mask preview, and export to 'GeoJSON', 'QuPath', and 'TIFF' formats. A versioned partner contract exchanges hash-inventoried handoff directories, deep-learning training datasets and typed commands over an optional local control service.
